Where the evidence is kept
Two columns. On the left, the audit trail shipped to an aggregator: somebody
else owns the store, it is retained on their dial rather than yours, and one
day the contract ends — three ways for the evidence to be missing on the day
somebody asks. On the right, the trail as records in the tenant's own store:
on its change feed like everything else, exported and restored with it, and
with no interface that edits an entry, for anybody, including the party
running the deployment.
